---
// Le due direzioni di un vertical coordinate system e l'errore che nasce mescolandole.
---

<figure class="my-8">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 700 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="verso-title" class="h-auto w-full text-foreground">
    <title id="verso-title">
      A sinistra le due convenzioni, positive up e positive down. A destra l'effetto di leggere dati
      batimetrici come se fossero altezze: il fondale risale sopra la costa.
    </title>

    <text x="190" y="44" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">le due convenzioni</text>
    <text x="540" y="44" font-size="13" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">mescolarle</text>

    <!-- convenzioni -->
    <line x1="50" y1="155" x2="330" y2="155" class="stroke-muted-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />

    <line x1="120" y1="90" x2="120" y2="220" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <line x1="115" y1="90" x2="125" y2="90" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <line x1="115" y1="220" x2="125" y2="220" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="132" y="94" font-size="11" class="fill-foreground">+30</text>
    <text x="132" y="159" font-size="11" class="fill-muted-foreground">0</text>
    <text x="132" y="224" font-size="11" class="fill-foreground">−30</text>
    <text x="120" y="76" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">positive up</text>
    <text x="120" y="248" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground">altezze</text>

    <line x1="260" y1="90" x2="260" y2="220" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <line x1="255" y1="90" x2="265" y2="90" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <line x1="255" y1="220" x2="265" y2="220" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="1.5" />
    <text x="272" y="94" font-size="11" class="fill-foreground">−30</text>
    <text x="272" y="159" font-size="11" class="fill-muted-foreground">0</text>
    <text x="272" y="224" font-size="11" class="fill-foreground">+30</text>
    <text x="260" y="76" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-foreground">positive down</text>
    <text x="260" y="248" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground">profondità</text>

    <text x="52" y="174" font-size="10" class="fill-muted-foreground">superficie di riferimento</text>

    <!-- l'errore -->
    <line x1="400" y1="185" x2="680" y2="185" class="stroke-muted-foreground" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="6 4" />
    <path d="M 400 120 L 450 138 L 500 165 L 530 185" fill="none" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="2.5" />
    <path d="M 530 185 L 580 210 L 630 232 L 675 245" fill="none" class="stroke-muted-foreground" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4" />
    <path d="M 530 185 L 580 160 L 630 138 L 675 125" fill="none" class="stroke-foreground" stroke-width="2.5" />

    <text x="430" y="110" font-size="10.5" class="fill-muted-foreground">costa</text>
    <text x="678" y="266" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" class="fill-muted-foreground">fondale vero</text>
    <text x="678" y="118" font-size="10.5" text-anchor="end" class="fill-foreground">fondale disegnato</text>
    <text x="540" y="278" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" class="fill-muted-foreground">i valori sono corretti, il verso no</text>
  </svg>
  <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
    Un sistema verticale porta due informazioni: l'unità, sempre lineare, e la
    <strong class="font-medium text-foreground">direzione</strong>. La direzione è quella che si
    dimentica, e il caso peggiore è il più silenzioso: un dataset batimetrico <em>positive down</em>
    sovrapposto a uno topografico <em>positive up</em> produce un fondale che risale sopra la costa,
    con tutti i valori numericamente giusti. Il difetto è nella lettura, non nel dato.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
